# General Development Rules

- **Language:** TypeScript only. Avoid `any` types; use explicit interfaces from `src/types/`.
- **Modularity:** Keep functions and components small and focused (< 250 lines).
- **No Duplicate Logic:** Reuse existing components from `src/components/` and context hooks from `src/context/`.
- **Surgical Edits:** Never modify unrelated files or change syllabus JSON structures unless specifically requested.
- **Context Awareness:** Before making changes, always review `docs/PRD.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/DESIGN.md`, and `docs/RULES.md`.
